Revision history for Unblock-HTTP2

0.001  Not yet released
    - Start standalone event-loop and operating-system neutral HTTP/2 engine.
    - Use Uniform::HTTP 0.04 Request and Response objects directly.
    - Add byte-in/byte-out Client and Server engines with no socket ownership.
    - Add multiplexed Stream objects, streaming request/response bodies,
      cooperative backpressure, cancellation, GOAWAY drain state, and decoded
      header-list limits.
    - Preserve application-owned outgoing Uniform messages without stamping a
      transport-selected version onto them.
    - Map received message lifecycle with freeze_initial(), trailers, and final
      completion/freeze semantics.
    - Add first-class request and response trailers over trailing HEADERS.
    - Add ordinary CONNECT and generic Extended CONNECT :protocol mapping.
    - Advertise SETTINGS_ENABLE_CONNECT_PROTOCOL on the server by default.
    - Add graceful client/server GOAWAY draining while allowing accepted streams
      to finish.
    - Replace Net::HTTP2::nghttp2 with a small private XS binding to libnghttp2,
      built through Alien::nghttp2.
    - Query effective peer SETTINGS for Extended CONNECT and remote stream
      concurrency enforcement.
    - Add Stream->inform() for one or more non-final informational Responses.
    - Preserve received GOAWAY last-stream-id, error code, and debug data.
    - Add application-driven receive flow control with per-stream consume()
      credit while keeping connection-level credit independent.
    - Add a public SETTINGS control plane with initial configuration, effective
      peer/local views, later updates, peer-change notifications, ACK tracking,
      RFC value validation, and no private nghttp2 session access.
    - Add connection-level PING with exact eight-byte opaque payloads, distinct
      PING/PING-ACK callbacks, automatic protocol ACKs, and no keepalive policy.
    - Add RFC 9218 extensible prioritization with
      SETTINGS_NO_RFC7540_PRIORITIES, ordinary Priority headers,
      client Stream->update_priority(), and server on_priority observation.
    - Add symmetric on_invalid_frame observation for protocol-invalid
      frames while retaining nghttp2's automatic RST_STREAM/GOAWAY handling.
    - Verify unknown extension frame types are ignored as required by HTTP/2.
    - Stop routing nghttp2's debug-only error callback through public server
      on_error.
    - Add explicit goaway() control with HTTP/2 error codes, binary debug data,
      local GOAWAY introspection, and non-increasing last-stream boundaries.
    - Route drain() through the same GOAWAY control path.
    - Close the engine deterministically when nghttp2 memory I/O reports a
      fatal failure, retain close_reason(), and still rethrow to the caller.
    - Enforce SETTINGS_ENABLE_PUSH as client-to-server only; servers now reject
      the setting even when the attempted value is zero.
    - Correct the documented public SETTINGS list to include
      no_rfc7540_priorities.
    - Tighten outbound pseudo-header validation so ordinary requests cannot
      emit an empty :path and Extended CONNECT cannot emit an empty :protocol.
    - Preserve RST_STREAM error codes with public RFC constants,
      Stream->reset(), error_code/error_name/reset_by_peer accessors, and
      reset codes passed through error callbacks for higher-layer retry policy.
    - Advertise ENABLE_PUSH = 0 until server push has a public Unblock model.
    - Add in-memory client/server protocol tests with no socket or event loop,
      including trailers and Extended CONNECT.
    - Add release packaging metadata, explicit MANIFEST and generated-file
      ignore rules.
    - Separate test-only prerequisites from runtime prerequisites.
    - Add CI distcheck/disttest coverage for the generated CPAN distribution.
    - Clean README Markdown rendering and add release-facing installation and
      status information.
    - Add CI-only bidirectional interoperability coverage against the
      independent nghttp2 nghttpd server and nghttp client.
